4. Data under other licences

  cad_agent/materials.py takes values from eight FreeCAD material cards (src/Mod/Material/
  Resources/Materials/Standard/...), each under the licence it names:

      Steel-Generic       Juergen Riegel      CC-BY-3.0
      ABS                 Juergen Riegel      CC-BY-3.0
      PLA                 Uwe Stöhr           CC-BY-3.0
      Polyamide 6         Uwe Stöhr           CC-BY-3.0
      Acrylic Glass       Przemo Firszt       CC-BY-3.0
      Aluminum Generic    Uwe Stöhr           LGPL-2.1-or-later
      Copper Generic      Uwe Stöhr           LGPL-2.1-or-later
      X5CrNi18-10         M. Münch            LGPL-2.0-or-later

  CC BY 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/) asks for the author's name, the title of
  the work, the licence and a credit for the use. materials.credit() writes them, and they are
  printed wherever a value of one of those cards is: in each row of `cad tables materials`, as
  `credits` in `cad tables` and `cad tables density`, and after the source of Young's modulus in a
  [[deflection]] row. The licence text is in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES. No card is copied: the numbers
  are, as the card gives them and cited to the card.

  The FreeCAD-library parts that `cad lib fetch` can download (CC-BY-3.0) and the ISO fasteners
  drawn by bd_warehouse (Apache-2.0) are not in this repository or in the wheel. They are fetched
  or installed on the user's side, and the library copies the credit the licence asks for into a
  part's sidecar (`attribution`). The Apache-2.0 text is in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.


5. Where the notices are

  LICENSE                      the MIT text (the cad-agent code)
  NOTICE                       this file
  THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES         the BSD, MIT, Zlib, CC0, CC-BY, CC-BY-SA and Apache texts
  ui/LICENSE                   the LGPL-2.1 text, and the statement for ui/
  ui/NOTICE                    the FreeCAD authors and files the UI follows
  cad_agent/workbench/next/    LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, written by the build
                               of the UI, so the bundle carries its notices when it is copied

  The wheel carries all of them: pyproject.toml lists the first five under license-files, which put
  them in the wheel's .dist-info/licenses, and the three files of cad_agent/workbench/next/ in the
  package data.
